---
import { waHref } from '../data/whatsapp.js';
// VISUAILS — /custom-models, "Your Brand Model".
//
// One component for both languages, same reason as StartPage / PricingPage /
// HomePage: the brief requires every change to land in EN and NL together, and
// one source file is the only way to guarantee that rather than merely intend
// it.
//
// THIS PAGE WAS A MERGE, and no longer entirely is. /models and
// /custom-models were two pages telling one story (AUDIT-TASK-0.md §D); §H·8
// folded /models into this page as a secondary #standard block and 301'd the
// old URL here. Lucas asked it back as its own page (task #268, 2026-07-29 —
// see AUDIT-TASK-0.md §H·8's own addendum for the full reasoning): the
// standard roster is now ALSO its own page at /models, sharing this page's
// roster data (src/data/models.js) rather than duplicating it. This page
// keeps a four-model taste of that roster under #standard, still reachable
// by the old fragment link, with a link to the full ten at /models — a
// visitor who wants the exclusive argument this page makes is not forced
// through the whole roster to get it, and a visitor who wants the roster
// is not forced through the whole exclusive argument either.
//
// WHAT CHANGED IN THE MERGE, and why:
//   · The "Why not just prompt a generic AI tool?" panel → REMOVED. It showed
//     one of our own renders under the label "Generic AI tool" with three
//     invented failings attached to it. The brief's rule is "never invent
//     testimonials, client names, logos, metrics, or results", and a fabricated
//     picture of a competitor's output is an invented result even when the alt
//     text admits it is a simulation. The same construct came off the homepage
//     for the same reason. The argument survives as prose about what we
//     actually do, and /compare is the page that owns the tool comparison
//     (§H·5 keeps that page's AI section alive precisely so this one does not
//     have to fake it).
//   · "A one-time design fee, then the normal visual price forever" → the real
//     numbers, read from pricing.js: setup, and the credit that returns it.
//     A page that says "a fee" without saying which fee is asking to be
//     distrusted by a brand that is about to spend four figures.
//   · Every CTA pointed at /order-custom. That page is deleted; the CTAs point
//     at /start, and /order-custom is a 301 to it in public/_redirects.
//   · /models' `#standard` roster lives here as a four-model taste (the full
//     ten moved to /models itself, task #268). Its per-model links used to be
//     /order?model=NAME query strings into a funnel that no longer exists;
//     the roster is now a library you look at, and the order happens at /start.
//     Nothing carries a model through a URL any more — /start's pipeline reads
//     no query state at all, by design (src/scripts/pipeline.js).
//   · The roster thumbnails were 60px squares in a card. They are portraits of
//     people and they are the actual product, so they are shown at a size you
//     can judge a face at. Square, never circular (§D).
//
// EVERY EURO ON THIS PAGE IS READ FROM src/data/pricing.js. Nothing is typed,
// and every printed price carries a VAT label from vatLabel() — BRIEF-14's
// hardest rule, and this page prints four figures.
//
// WHAT THE AUGUST 2026 MODEL CHANGED HERE, AND WHAT IT DID NOT (section 0 of
// src/data/pricing.js is the governing document):
//
//   · THE PRODUCT IS UNCHANGED BY THE LADDER. A Brand Model is a one-time setup
//     at AMOUNT.brandModel; none of the argument on this page is retired by the
//     move from packages to a per-product rate.
//     ── EN OP 23 AUGUSTUS 2026 IS DE CREDIT WÉL VERDWENEN. Hier stond dat de
//     setup zichzelf precies aflost via AMOUNT.brandModelCredit over
//     BRAND_MODEL_CREDIT_DROPS bestellingen. Dat klopt niet meer: het merkmodel
//     is één bedrag van € 450 dat je één keer betaalt, en er komt niets terug.
//     Zie de noot bij AMOUNT.brandModel in pricing.js en MERKMODEL-ONTWERP.md.
//   · WHERE THE NUMBERS CAME FROM IS NOT. They were read out of PACKAGES —
//     the two drop packages and the retainer — via a byId lookup, and PACKAGES
//     describes a price list we no longer sell. The setup fee, its unit and
//     its four inclusions are now built here from AMOUNT and the credit count,
//     which is where they were always really from; PACKAGES only wrapped them.
//   · "Whole drops — 25–30 products" was a package band. There is no band now;
//     the ladder prices every count. The row names the count at which an order
//     gets the reserved window instead, because that is the real line an order
//     crosses.
//   · THE WORD "DROP" IS GONE from everything we sell. It means a collection
//     going live to the brands we sell to, and this page used it for a work
//     order eleven times over — including in the H1. What we sell is an order;
//     in Dutch, een bestelling. The client’s own launch keeps the word.
import {
  AMOUNT, euro, vatLabel,
  WINDOW_THRESHOLD,
} from '../data/pricing.js';
import { ROSTER, rosterWoord, telwoord } from '../data/models.js';
import { localizedPath } from '../i18n/ui.js';
import Placeholder from './Placeholder.astro';

import ServiceSwitch from './ServiceSwitch.astro';
import '../styles/stijl22.css';
interface Props { lang: 'en' | 'nl'; }
const { lang } = Astro.props;
const lp = (p: string) => localizedPath(lang, p);

// The Brand Model, assembled here rather than looked up out of PACKAGES.
//
// It used to be `byId['brand-model']` off the package list, which meant this
// page's headline number arrived via a table of two drop packages and a
// retainer — none of which exist any more. The three facts it actually needs
// are the setup fee, its unit and its inclusions, and all three are either an
// AMOUNT or a sentence about the product. Built as one object so the template
// below is unchanged in shape, and so a missing piece is a build error rather
// than an empty price band on a page whose whole job is a number.
const brandModel = {
  price: euro(AMOUNT.brandModel, lang),
  /* DE EENHEID ZEGT IETS ANDERS DAN HET LABEL ERBOVEN. Hier stond
     "one-time setup" — precies het woord dat `costSetupLabel` er twee regels
     hoger al zet, dus las het blok als "One-time setup · € 450 · one-time setup
     · excl. VAT". De eenheid vertelt nu waar het bedrag over gáát: per merk, en
     niet per bestelling of per beeld. Dat is sinds 23 augustus het enige dat de
     lezer nog hoeft te weten — de tweede kolom die het terugverdienen uitlegde,
     is met de credit verdwenen. */
  unit: lang === 'nl' ? 'per merk' : 'per brand',
  includes: lang === 'nl'
    ? [
        'Eén gezicht per ontwerp, gebouwd voor jouw merk en door niemand anders gebruikt — wil je er meer, dan is elk gezicht een eigen ontwerp tegen hetzelfde bedrag',
        'Hetzelfde gezicht door een hele bestelling heen — en jij kiest per bestelling welk gezicht erop staat',
        'De uniekheidscontrole vóór levering: het gezicht gaat door gezichtszoekmachines en dat wordt op je bestelling vastgelegd. Blijkt het ooit toch op een bestaande persoon te lijken, dan ontwerpen we het opnieuw en maken we de bestelde beelden ermee over',
        'Blijft meegaan als je collectie verandert, en blijft aan jouw merk gekoppeld — ook als je een tijd niet bestelt',
      ]
    : [
        'One face per design, built for your brand and used by no one else — want more, then each face is its own design at the same amount',
        'The same face across a whole order — and you pick per order which face runs',
        'The uniqueness check before delivery: the face goes through face search engines and that is recorded on your order. Should it ever turn out to resemble a real person, we redesign it and remake the ordered images with it',
        'Kept current as your line changes, and tied to your brand — even if you do not order for a while',
      ],
};

// The standard library. Was defined inline here; moved to src/data/models.js
// (task #268) the day /models became a real page again, so both pages read
// the same ten names and photo paths instead of maintaining two copies.
// ROSTER's own trait KEYS are shared too — only the label translation
// (COPY[lang].traits below) still lives per-page, because that half really
// is page-local UI copy, not a fact about the roster.
//
// Below the fold on THIS page, ROSTER is sliced to a four-model taste — see
// the #standard section — so the two pages are not indexing the same ten
// portraits twice; the full ten live at /models now.

// Our own finished work. Not before/afters, not client results — output.
// Intrinsic sizes, per photo, because these four are NOT all the same shape:
// 01 and 02 are 800x1071, 04 and 05 are 1200x1200. One shared width/height on
// the <img> reserved a square box for two portraits, which is layout shift.
/* De zes gedeelde gezichten achter het merkmodel in de hero. Kleine derivaten
   (380px, zie scripts/make-thumbs.mjs): ze worden getekend in vakjes van
   ongeveer 150 px en de hero is het eerste wat binnenkomt. */
const WALL = ['aaron', 'ava', 'elias', 'ryan', 'dana', 'rae']
  .map((n) => ({ src: `/img/model-${n}-w380.webp`, w: 380, h: 509 }));

const EXAMPLES = [
  { src: '/img/custom-models-01.webp', w: 800, h: 1071 },
  /* -02 staat sinds 4 september in de hero (zie de noot daar) en -03 is Rae uit
     de standaardbibliotheek — een gedeeld gezicht hoort niet in een raster dat
     "echt geleverd werk" heet op de pagina over exclusieve gezichten. */
  { src: '/img/custom-models-04.webp', w: 1200, h: 1200 },
  { src: '/img/custom-models-05.webp', w: 1200, h: 1200 },
  /* ── EN HIER STONDEN DEZELFDE TWEE MENSEN NOG EEN KEER — 4 september 2026 ──
     model-raw-01 en model-raw-02 zijn andere BESTANDEN dan custom-models-04 en
     -05, maar het zijn dezelfde twee gezichten in een andere uitsnede. In een
     raster van zes stonden dus vier mensen, waarvan twee dubbel — op de sectie
     die "echt geleverd werk" heet. Vier verschillende gezichten zeggen wat zes
     met twee dubbelgangers niet zeggen. */
];

// ── Copy ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Prose only. Every euro, every count, every promise about an order comes out
// of pricing.js in both languages.
//
// No `as const`: COPY[lang] on a union of two readonly object literals gives
// readonly tuple unions, and .map() on those is a TS error. See StartPage.
/* Hoeveel roostergezichten deze pagina als voorproefje toont. Als getal, want de
   bibliotheeknoot eronder noemt het én de slice verderop gebruikt het — en die twee
   liepen tot 3 september 2026 los van elkaar: de noot zei "Drie van de tien" en de
   slice had kunnen veranderen zonder dat de zin meebewoog. */
